Wanted: a top-level activity read, graphed rather than tabulated. Candidates, cheapest first:
- work items closed per day across the fleet, stacked by outcome (already in the issue reads — no new requests);
- commits to each member&#39;s default branch per day (`/repos/{r}/commits` is one call per member, or free from the existing head-sha read at day granularity);
- runs per day and their pass rate;
- which members moved at all — a fleet where two of twelve are active is a fact about the fleet.

Constraint that shapes it: it must come from reads the page **already makes**, or it undoes #995. Anything needing a per-member extra call has to justify itself against the anonymous 60/hour case.","state":"open","html_url":"https://github.com/missingbulb/Claudinite/issues/999","user":{"login":"missingbulb","id":73882448,"profile_url":"https://github.com/missingbulb","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73882448?v=4"},"author_association":"OWNER","reactions":{"total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"created_at":"2026-08-18T14:01:41Z","updated_at":"2026-08-18T14:01:41Z","has_parent":false,"has_children":false,"closed_by_pull_requests":{"total_count":1,"references":[{"number":1008,"title":"dashboard: digests, a fleet activity read, the grid split, and what the machinery bought","state":"OPEN","url":"https://github.com/missingbulb/Claudinite/pull/1008","repository":"missingbulb/Claudinite"}]}}

